      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-464",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "If we let $u=\\dfrac x 3,$ then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = \\dfrac 1 3\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d x =3\\, \\textrm d u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{x}{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\operatorname{sin}\u2061u\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3\\int \\operatorname{sin}\u2061u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-6\\operatorname{cos}\u2061u+C \\\\  & =-6\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{x}{3})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/example-464.json",
