      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-466",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Let $u = x^3 - \\dfrac{\\pi}{6}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d} u}{\\textrm{d}x } = 3x^2 \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\dfrac 1 3 \\textrm d u = x^2\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}{sec}^{2}\u2061({x}^{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {sec}^{2}\u2061({x}^{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\cdot {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}\u2061(u)\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int {sec}^{2}\u2061(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tan}\u2061u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tan}\u2061({x}^{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006406/example-466.json",
          "file_sha256": "5dbaf0265d1b13acc93a79d12579459a43bdeefc079da41aeda10848648bd77e"
